# CVE-2026-98432: the IPv4 TCP SYN path frees IP options while a child socket
# still uses them. OpenWrt 25.12.6 ships kernel 6.12.112; the fix is 6.12.113.
# Legitimate TCP does not carry IP options, so drop them before conntrack and
# routing (Red Hat's RHSB-2026-016 mitigation). Once the routers run a fixed
# kernel, drop the imports, then delete the file and reload firewall4 on each
# router by hand:
# Dewclaw cannot remove files and sysupgrade keeps /etc/nftables.d.
chain drop_tcp_ip_options {
	type filter hook prerouting priority -310; policy accept;
	ip protocol tcp ip hdrlength > 5 counter drop
}
